preConditionHook:
// THE PREMARKET EXTREMES AS LEVELS. The high and low made in the overnight /
// premarket window are carried into the day session and tested there: Brooks
// treats them as magnets that usually get tested once the day session opens.
// The LONG is the test of the premarket high (the bar's high reaches to
// within toleranceTicks of it), the SHORT the mirror at the premarket low,
// exactly as the merged pseudocode spells the long side.
//
// SESSION MODEL per the standing decision: the session starts when the bar's
// wall-clock close date changes -- EL date > date[1], mirrored as
// day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)) as SessionOpenPriceTarget and
// DailyPivotProximity write it -- and the premarket accumulators reset there.
// The premarket WINDOW inside that session is a clock-time band: bars whose
// close Time is after premarketStart and at or before premarketEnd. EL Time
// is VERIFIED as the bar's closing HHMM on the exchange clock (a midnight bar
// reads 0, not 2400), and ctx.Time(n) is that same close timestamp, so HHMM
// is its seconds-of-day repacked -- KeyTimeProximity's derivation, carried
// here unchanged. The defaults 300 and 630 are the 03:00-06:30 premarket
// preceding an 06:30 regular open: a band wholly inside one wall-clock date,
// which is what lets the date-change reset serve it.
//
// havePm IS THE WARM-UP AND FEED GUARD, and it carries real content: on a
// regular-session-only series NO bar falls in the window, havePm never turns
// true, and the rule is silent rather than testing a zero level (EL variables
// hold their initial 0 until first assigned, and 0 as a price sits under
// every real price). The rule needs a feed that includes the Globex /
// overnight bars.
//
// pastPremarket keeps the rule from firing on the premarket bars themselves,
// where the running extreme IS the current bar's own high and the test would
// be trivially true on every new extreme.
//
// The extremes accumulate with plain comparisons rather than MaxList /
// MinList so the two twins read statement for statement; the running value is
// seeded from the window's FIRST bar rather than from 0, which is what makes
// pmLow meaningful.
//
// SAME SHAPE AS PriorSessionLevelTest but a different level: that rule tests
// the PREVIOUS session's high / low / close within an ATR band, this one a
// level built inside the CURRENT session's own overnight window within a TICK
// band -- the tick is why it was held for this list. INTRADAY ONLY: on a
// daily or 1440-minute series a bar's close time is the session close, no bar
// lands in the premarket band, and the rule never fires.
//
// The tick is ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale(), division-first, both VERIFIED
// and per-symbol constant for the run.
//
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a
// redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy. pmHigh, pmLow
// and havePm are the cross-bar state and are deliberately NOT reset each bar.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
barSeconds = seconds_of_day(ctx.Time(0));
barHHMM = (barSeconds / 3600) * 100 + (barSeconds % 3600) / 60;
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    pmHigh = 0.0;
    pmLow = 0.0;
    havePm = false;
}
inPremarket = el_gt((double)barHHMM, premarketStart) && el_le((double)barHHMM, premarketEnd);
if (inPremarket) {
    if (havePm) {
        if (el_gt(high[0], pmHigh)) pmHigh = high[0];
        if (el_lt(low[0], pmLow)) pmLow = low[0];
    } else {
        pmHigh = high[0];
        pmLow = low[0];
        havePm = true;
    }
}
pastPremarket = el_gt((double)barHHMM, premarketEnd);
